<div class="paragraph paragraph--type--bp-columns paragraph--view-mode--default paragraph--width--wide">
  <div class="paragraph__column ">
    <div class="paragraph__column--container-wrapper">
  <div class="container"><div class="paragraph--type--bp-columns__1col">
      


    
    
        
    
    
    

    
    
    
    
    
    

        <div class="paragraph__card paragraph paragraph--type--card-basic card_border paragraph--view-mode--default">
            <div class="paragraph__column">
                <div class="paragraph__title title_color color__brand-dark-blue  ">
                    <h3 class="mt-0 mb-0">
                        
                    </h3>
                </div>
                
            <div class="field field--name-field-card-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field--item"><h2 class="text-align-center">About Colorado Charitable Organizations</h2><p>Colorado allows charitable organizations to be exempt from state-collected sales tax for purchases made in the conduct of their regular charitable functions and activities. [§39-26-718 (1) (a), C.R.S.] Organizations that are&nbsp;<a href="https://www.irs.gov/charities-non-profits/charitable-organizations/exemption-requirements-501c3-organizations" target="_blank">exempt from federal income tax under 501(c)(3)</a>&nbsp;will generally be approved for a Certificate of Exemption in Colorado. For more information, review the <a href="/tax-exemption-qualifications" target="_blank">Tax Exemption Qualification Criteria</a> web page and&nbsp;<a href="/income-tax-topics-charitable-contributions" target="_blank" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="aa2927ef-001d-41e9-a09f-6e1b058023a8" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Income Tax Topics: Charitable Contributions">Charitable Organization</a>&nbsp;guidance publication.</p><p>Select an option above for more&nbsp;information on&nbsp;charitable and nonprofit organizations. This information also applies to government agencies and certain religious organizations. However, this information does not apply to self-collecting taxation jurisdictions. Self-collecting jurisdictions establish their own tax regulations, and collect their own sales/use tax.</p><p>Please contact each self-collecting jurisdiction directly for information about the tax regulations in that jurisdiction. Visit the&nbsp;<a href="/local-government-sales-tax" target="_blank" title="Local Government Sales Tax">Local Government Sales Tax</a>&nbsp;web page for more information about self-collecting jurisdictions.</p><p><strong>NOTE: Use the&nbsp;</strong><a href="https://dor-taxdonations.uc.r.appspot.com/" target="_blank"><strong>Charity Lookup Tool</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;to find the identification number of a Colorado charitable organization (nonprofit fund) for the Voluntary Contributions Schedule (</strong><a href="/individual-income-tax-forms" target="_blank" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="ae6f3710-da38-4592-9875-7fe69561af6a" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Income Tax Forms for Individuals &amp; Families"><strong>DR 0104CH</strong></a><strong>) on your Individual Income Tax Return (DR 0104).</strong></p><p class="text-align-center">&nbsp;</p><div class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/jE6XaCKva-0?si=oWQNQ3aXoZcGSkVp" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><p>&nbsp;</p></div>
      
                
            </div>
    </div>

    </div></div>
</div>
  </div>
</div>

</div>
  
  </div>

</div>


  </div>


